.netlify

# .agents/: az install sajat termek-/marketing-kontextusa -- KERESKEDELMI ADAT
# (arak, pozicionalas, versenytarsak), SOHA nem mehet a repoba. Tartalom-szintu
# ignore (".agents/*", nem ".agents/"), mert konyvtar-szintu kizaras utan a
# fajl-negacio nem hat (ld. 8811abfd, a .claude/settings.json ugyanigy romlott
# el). A .example vaz viszont kimegy: abbol kap a vevo sajat kontextus-sablont.
.agents/*
!.agents/product-marketing.md.example

# Upload staging area written into the install directory: per-install state,
# not source. (The UI language marker .lang this commit also added has since
# landed on develop; kept there, not duplicated here.)
.uploads/

# Scratch HOME for test runs. The suite is run as `HOME=<scratch> npx vitest`
# because #1348 -- before it, the full suite wrote into the owner's real
# ~/.ssh/authorized_keys. The tool leaves droppings in that HOME (npm's
# update-notifier stamp, a 648 KB lbdb vector extension), and three PRs in the
# MEMKERESVAK917 series would have carried the first of them into the repo.
# No trailing slash on purpose: a trailing slash does not match a symlink, so
# `.fakehome/` would stop ignoring it the day the scratch HOME is created as one.
.fakehome

# Supabase CLI scratch state (cli-latest, linked-project.json). Written on every
# CLI run, never source. Two of these rode into #1324 and would have been the
# first ones in the repo -- after that they regenerate silently on every run.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, same rule and same reason as `.fakehome` above, measured
# again for this path on 2026-09-17 in a throwaway repo, with an empty-.gitignore
# negative control confirming the file is visible when unignored:
#   supabase/.temp   -> ignores a real directory AND a symlink
#   supabase/.temp/  -> ignores a real directory, MISSES the symlink (it shows in
#                       `git status`, so the next CLI run commits it again)
supabase/.temp
